# Cloudflare Pages reads this file at deploy time. It is not served to anyone.
#
# ⚠ RULES ARE ADDITIVE — A LATER RULE DOES NOT REPLACE AN EARLIER ONE, IT APPENDS TO
# IT. Measured, not assumed; see the Cache-Control note below for what that cost.
# So a header must be set in exactly ONE block, never in two.

# ⚠ NO Cache-Control IN THE CATCH-ALL. Cloudflare APPENDS matching rules rather than
# overriding them, so setting it here AND on /assets/* produced the header
#   Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate, public, max-age=31536000, immutable
# on every asset — measured on the live deployment. A client reading the first
# max-age revalidates everything, which is the exact opposite of what the second half
# asks for. Pages already defaults HTML to `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`
# (verified against the live response), so leaving it unset here gets the right
# behaviour for HTML and lets /assets/* own the only Cache-Control on the page.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), interest-cohort=()

  # ⚠ `form-action` AND `connect-src` ARE THE LOAD-BEARING DIRECTIVES HERE, and they
  # are why this is worth having on a static page at all: they pin the signup to Kit
  # and nowhere else, so no injected script can quietly repoint the email form at
  # somebody else's endpoint. If the wishlist ever stops working after a deploy,
  # THIS LINE IS THE FIRST SUSPECT — check the browser console for a CSP violation
  # before touching the JavaScript.
  # 'unsafe-inline' is present because the page's CSS and JS are deliberately inline
  # (one request, no build step); it weakens script-src but not the two directives
  # above, which are the ones protecting the visitor's address.
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data:; media-src 'self'; connect-src https://app.kit.com; form-action https://app.kit.com; base-uri 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'

/assets/*
  # Safe to pin for a year because every asset that can change is requested with a
  # ?v= query, and the browser caches on the full URL. Bump the ?v= in index.html
  # when you replace a file in place.
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
